  "created": "2026-10-08T19:52:11.75Z",
  "description": "Transport-neutral telemetry facade for Orleans.Lattice. Implements the ILatticeTelemetry contract over a curated, server-authored named-query catalogue that is selected by id and never accepts raw PromQL from any caller, scopes every evaluation to a tenant the facade derives server-side from the authenticated caller (honouring a cross-tenant or single-tenant request only after platform-operator validation and otherwise degrading fail-closed), and executes through the read-only Prometheus / PromQL-compatible backend client. Also holds the dual-credential trust boundary that stamps the configured backend credential and never a caller's Lattice credential, the range and step guardrails, and the fail-closed metric-access allow-list. Depends on no transport, so every binding (the MCP tool group, the gRPC service, and client heads) adapts over the same machinery instead of forking it.",
  "id": "Orleans.Lattice.Api.Telemetry",
